From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] display: never unblank to brightness -1

set_brightness, the brightness to unblank to, stays -1 until the
display brightness pipe has run while the display is on. At boot the
pipe runs while the display still counts as off; the brightness filter
chokes it (returns 0) and display_brightness_trigger() drops the value.
The first unblank after locking then wrote -1 ("4294967295") to the
backlight's brightness file, which the kernel rejects with EINVAL, so
the backlight stayed at 0: on the Nokia N950 the display stayed dark
after the first lock, while mce reported it on and unlocked. Changing
the brightness setting once while the display is on hid the problem
until the next boot.

Before unblanking, run the pipe again if set_brightness is unset, and
fall back to the setting's 20 % steps if the filter still chokes it.

Found with strace on the N950: write(13, "4294967295", 10) = -1 EINVAL.
---
--- a/src/modules/display.c
+++ b/src/modules/display.c
@@ -221,10 +221,37 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * The brightness to unblank to
+ *
+ * set_brightness stays -1 until the brightness pipe has run while the
+ * display is on. At boot it runs while the display still counts as off,
+ * the brightness filter chokes it (0) and the value is dropped; the first
+ * unblank after locking then wrote -1, which the backlight rejects, and
+ * the display stayed dark. Run the pipe again now, and fall back to the
+ * setting's 20 % steps if it is still choked.
+ *
+ * @return The brightness to use, never negative
+ */
+static gint unblank_brightness(void)
+{
+	if (set_brightness < 0)
+		(void)execute_datapipe(&display_brightness_pipe,
+				       GINT_TO_POINTER(set_brightness_unfiltered),
+				       USE_INDATA, CACHE_INDATA);
+
+	if (set_brightness < 0)
+		set_brightness = (maximum_display_brightness *
+				  CLAMP(set_brightness_unfiltered, 1, 5) * 20) / 100;
+
+	return set_brightness;
+}
+
+/**
  * Unblank display
  */
 static void display_unblank(void)
 {
+	(void)unblank_brightness();
 	/* If we unblank, switch on display immediately */
 	if (cached_brightness == 0) {
 		cached_brightness = set_brightness;
